{
  "title": "Is button B really better?",
  "setting": "Day 1 at BrightCart",
  "mission": "Decide whether to recommend the new checkout button. **Tell the team what the test does—and does not—show.**",
  "deadline": "Checkout review today at 3 pm",
  "panels": [
    {
      "title": "One day of test results",
      "metrics": [
        {
          "label": "Visits per version",
          "value": "1,200",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "label": "Conversion (A / B)",
          "value": "4.0% / 5.0%",
          "note": "48 orders on A; 60 on B"
        }
      ],
      "note": "Visitors were split between the current button (A) and the new button (B)."
    }
  ],
  "team": [
    {
      "id": "data",
      "role": "Data scientist",
      "expertise": "Checks whether a difference could be chance and advises on test size.",
      "ai": false
    },
    {
      "id": "product",
      "role": "Product manager",
      "expertise": "Owns the checkout launch and wants to move quickly.",
      "ai": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ai",
      "role": "AI assistant",
      "expertise": "Can calculate a test check and summarize its limits when asked.",
      "ai": true
    }
  ],
  "meters": [
    {
      "id": "risk",
      "label": "Risk of a wrong call",
      "start": 55,
      "goodWhen": "low"
    },
    {
      "id": "patience",
      "label": "{{product}}'s patience",
      "start": 70,
      "goodWhen": "high"
    }
  ],
  "skills": [
    {
      "id": "chance",
      "name": "Tell a gap from chance",
      "practice": "Explain why a higher rate in one test group does not, by itself, prove a real difference."
    },
    {
      "id": "sample",
      "name": "Choose a sample size",
      "practice": "Write down how many visitors per version you would want before checking an A/B test."
    },
    {
      "id": "explain",
      "name": "Explain a test result",
      "practice": "Explain a test result to someone who isn't a data person, in one sentence."
    }
  ],
  "startNodeId": "start",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "start",
      "messages": [
        {
          "from": "product",
          "text": "B has one percentage point more conversions. Can we make it the default before the review?"
        },
        {
          "from": "data",
          "text": "The gap is worth checking, but one day is a small sample. A higher rate doesn't automatically mean B caused the difference."
        }
      ],
      "prompt": "How do you respond to the early results?",
      "choices": [
        {
          "id": "ask-ai",
          "text": "Ask the AI to check whether this gap could be chance.",
          "quality": "strong",
          "replies": [
            {
              "from": "ai",
              "text": "The quick check is about 0.24. In plain words, if the versions were really no different, a gap this large or larger wouldn't be surprising. This is not strong evidence yet."
            }
          ],
          "effects": [
            {
              "meter": "risk",
              "change": -8
            },
            {
              "meter": "patience",
              "change": -2
            }
          ],
          "timeJump": null,
          "notes": [
            {
              "skill": "chance",
              "kind": "good",
              "text": "You checked whether chance could explain the gap instead of treating a higher rate as proof.",
              "example": null
            },
            {
              "skill": "explain",
              "kind": "good",
              "text": "You used the check to give {{product}} a clear reason not to rush the call.",
              "example": null
            }
          ],
          "next": "plan"
        },
        {
          "id": "compare-rates",
          "text": "Compare the rates: B is at 5.0% and A is at 4.0%, but I won't call a winner yet.",
          "quality": "fair",
          "replies": [
            {
              "from": "data",
              "text": "Good to compare rates rather than just the order counts. We still need to check how much uncertainty there is."
            }
          ],
          "effects": [
            {
              "meter": "risk",
              "change": -2
            },
            {
              "meter": "patience",
              "change": -3
            }
          ],
          "timeJump": null,
          "notes": [
            {
              "skill": "chance",
              "kind": "good",
              "text": "You compared conversion rates and avoided calling the higher count a win.",
              "example": null
            },
            {
              "skill": "chance",
              "kind": "improve",
              "text": "To judge the gap, also check whether this sample is large enough to separate a real difference from chance.",
              "example": "“B is higher so far, but let's check whether the difference could be chance.”"
            }
          ],
          "next": "plan"
        },
        {
          "id": "ship-now",
          "text": "Tell {{product}} to switch everyone to B because it has more orders.",
          "quality": "weak",
          "replies": [
            {
              "from": "data",
              "text": "B had more orders, but it also had the same number of visits as A. We need to check whether the rate difference is more than chance."
            }
          ],
          "effects": [
            {
              "meter": "risk",
              "change": 15
            },
            {
              "meter": "patience",
              "change": 8
            }
          ],
          "timeJump": null,
          "notes": [
            {
              "skill": "chance",
              "kind": "improve",
              "text": "More orders alone don't settle the question. Compare rates, then check how uncertain the gap is.",
              "example": "“B is ahead so far, but I need to check whether that could be chance.”"
            }
          ],
          "next": "plan"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "plan",
      "messages": [
        {
          "from": "product",
          "text": "I can keep the test running, but each extra day delays the launch."
        },
        {
          "from": "data",
          "text": "More visitors can make the result clearer. We can plan a checkpoint rather than checking every few hours."
        }
      ],
      "prompt": "What checkpoint do you choose?",
      "choices": [
        {
          "id": "launch-early",
          "text": "Make B the default now and use the first day's results to guide the launch.",
          "quality": "weak",
          "replies": [
            {
              "from": "product",
              "text": "That gets us moving, though we won't know whether this early gap is more than chance."
            }
          ],
          "effects": [
            {
              "meter": "risk",
              "change": 15
            },
            {
              "meter": "patience",
              "change": 8
            }
          ],
          "timeJump": null,
          "notes": [
            {
              "skill": "sample",
              "kind": "improve",
              "text": "With only 1,200 visits per version, the test may not have enough observations to show a clear difference.",
              "example": "“Let's set a visitor target and check again when we reach it.”"
            }
          ],
          "next": "early"
        },
        {
          "id": "three-days",
          "text": "Keep the test running for about 3 more days, then check again.",
          "quality": "strong",
          "replies": [
            {
              "from": "data",
              "text": "That gives us a clear checkpoint without holding the launch longer than needed. We'll check the rates and whether the gap could be chance."
            }
          ],
          "effects": [
            {
              "meter": "risk",
              "change": -15
            },
            {
              "meter": "patience",
              "change": -10
            }
          ],
          "timeJump": {
            "label": "3 days later",
            "panel": {
              "title": "Checkpoint: 4 days of testing",
              "metrics": [
                {
                  "label": "Visits per version",
                  "value": "4,800",
                  "note": null
                },
                {
                  "label": "Conversion (A / B)",
                  "value": "4.0% / 5.0%",
                  "note": "192 orders on A; 240 on B"
                }
              ],
              "note": "The same 1,200 visits per version were added each day."
            }
          },
          "notes": [
            {
              "skill": "sample",
              "kind": "good",
              "text": "You chose a checkpoint that gives the comparison more observations while limiting the delay.",
              "example": null
            }
          ],
          "next": "full"
        },
        {
          "id": "six-days",
          "text": "Keep the test running for 6 more days for a larger sample before deciding.",
          "quality": "fair",
          "replies": [
            {
              "from": "data",
              "text": "A larger sample can give us more confidence, but it means a longer wait. The rates may still end up the same."
            }
          ],
          "effects": [
            {
              "meter": "risk",
              "change": -18
            },
            {
              "meter": "patience",
              "change": -20
            }
          ],
          "timeJump": {
            "label": "6 days later",
            "panel": {
              "title": "Checkpoint: 7 days of testing",
              "metrics": [
                {
                  "label": "Visits per version",
                  "value": "8,400",
                  "note": null
                },
                {
                  "label": "Conversion (A / B)",
                  "value": "4.0% / 5.0%",
                  "note": "336 orders on A; 420 on B"
                }
              ],
              "note": "The same 1,200 visits per version were added each day."
            }
          },
          "notes": [
            {
              "skill": "sample",
              "kind": "good",
              "text": "You planned a larger sample, which can make a small but steady gap easier to distinguish from chance.",
              "example": null
            },
            {
              "skill": "explain",
              "kind": "improve",
              "text": "A longer test has a cost too. Tell {{product}} why this extra wait is worth it.",
              "example": "“A larger sample may make the result clearer, but it will delay the launch by several days.”"
            }
          ],
          "next": "full"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "early",
      "messages": [
        {
          "from": "data",
          "text": "At 1,200 visits per version, the rates are still 4.0% and 5.0%. The quick chance check is about 0.24, so we can't rule out chance."
        },
        {
          "from": "product",
          "text": "Waiting costs time. Is there a way to move forward without claiming B has won?"
        }
      ],
      "prompt": "What do you recommend with only the first day's data?",
      "choices": [
        {
          "id": "keep-test",
          "text": "Keep the test running and don't call a winner yet.",
          "quality": "strong",
          "replies": [
            {
              "from": "data",
              "text": "That keeps the comparison fair while we gather more visits."
            }
          ],
          "effects": [
            {
              "meter": "risk",
              "change": -8
            },
            {
              "meter": "patience",
              "change": -10
            }
          ],
          "timeJump": null,
          "notes": [
            {
              "skill": "chance",
              "kind": "good",
              "text": "You treated an inconclusive result as a reason to keep learning, not as proof that the versions are equal.",
              "example": null
            },
            {
              "skill": "explain",
              "kind": "good",
              "text": "You gave a clear, honest recommendation instead of overstating the early result.",
              "example": "“B is ahead so far, but this sample can't rule out chance. Let's keep testing.”"
            }
          ],
          "next": "hold"
        },
        {
          "id": "small-pilot",
          "text": "Try B with a small share of visitors while the test keeps running.",
          "quality": "fair",
          "replies": [
            {
              "from": "product",
              "text": "That gives us a way to move carefully, though we should still avoid calling B a proven winner."
            }
          ],
          "effects": [
            {
              "meter": "risk",
              "change": 4
            },
            {
              "meter": "patience",
              "change": 5
            }
          ],
          "timeJump": null,
          "notes": [
            {
              "skill": "explain",
              "kind": "good",
              "text": "You offered a cautious next step without presenting the early gap as a sure thing.",
              "example": null
            },
            {
              "skill": "chance",
              "kind": "improve",
              "text": "Make clear that the test still needs more visitors before it can support a winner call.",
              "example": "“We can try B with a small share, but this early result could still be chance.”"
            }
          ],
          "next": "pilot"
        },
        {
          "id": "early-rollout",
          "text": "Switch everyone to B and report that the test shows it is better.",
          "quality": "weak",
          "replies": [
            {
              "from": "data",
              "text": "The observed rate is higher, but this sample doesn't give strong evidence that B is truly better."
            }
          ],
          "effects": [
            {
              "meter": "risk",
              "change": 15
            },
            {
              "meter": "patience",
              "change": 8
            }
          ],
          "timeJump": null,
          "notes": [
            {
              "skill": "explain",
              "kind": "improve",
              "text": "Saying the test shows B is better overstates an early, uncertain result.",
              "example": "“B is higher so far, but we need more data before we can say the gap is real.”"
            }
          ],
          "next": "broad"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "full",
      "messages": [
        {
          "from": "data",
          "text": "At this checkpoint, B is still at 5.0% and A at 4.0%. The difference clears the usual 5% chance check, whether we tested 4,800 or 8,400 visits per version."
        },
        {
          "from": "ai",
          "text": "That is evidence that the versions differ, not a guarantee that B will keep performing better in the future."
        },
        {
          "from": "product",
          "text": "Can we move ahead without making a promise the test can't support?"
        }
      ],
      "prompt": "What do you recommend after the larger sample?",
      "choices": [
        {
          "id": "measured-rollout",
          "text": "Roll B out to 20% of visitors and keep monitoring conversion.",
          "quality": "strong",
          "replies": [
            {
              "from": "product",
              "text": "That gives us a practical next step while keeping an eye on whether the result holds."
            }
          ],
          "effects": [
            {
              "meter": "risk",
              "change": -12
            },
            {
              "meter": "patience",
              "change": 6
            }
          ],
          "timeJump": null,
          "notes": [
            {
              "skill": "chance",
              "kind": "good",
              "text": "You used the larger sample and chance check to support a measured rollout, not a guarantee.",
              "example": null
            },
            {
              "skill": "explain",
              "kind": "good",
              "text": "You paired your recommendation with a way to keep checking the result.",
              "example": "“The test supports trying B with more visitors; let's monitor it as we roll it out.”"
            }
          ],
          "next": "pilot"
        },
        {
          "id": "wait-more",
          "text": "Keep the test running longer before changing the default.",
          "quality": "fair",
          "replies": [
            {
              "from": "data",
              "text": "That is cautious. The result already clears the usual check, so explain why more evidence is worth the extra delay."
            }
          ],
          "effects": [
            {
              "meter": "risk",
              "change": -4
            },
            {
              "meter": "patience",
              "change": -12
            }
          ],
          "timeJump": null,
          "notes": [
            {
              "skill": "sample",
              "kind": "good",
              "text": "You recognized that a larger sample could add confidence before a bigger change.",
              "example": null
            },
            {
              "skill": "explain",
              "kind": "improve",
              "text": "The longer test already passed the usual chance check. Say what remaining doubt another wait would address.",
              "example": "“The result supports B, but I'd like to check whether the lift holds over more time.”"
            }
          ],
          "next": "hold"
        },
        {
          "id": "guarantee",
          "text": "Switch everyone to B and promise it will keep getting better results.",
          "quality": "weak",
          "replies": [
            {
              "from": "ai",
              "text": "The test supports a difference in this experiment. It can't promise what will happen for every future visitor."
            }
          ],
          "effects": [
            {
              "meter": "risk",
              "change": 12
            },
            {
              "meter": "patience",
              "change": 8
            }
          ],
          "timeJump": null,
          "notes": [
            {
              "skill": "explain",
              "kind": "improve",
              "text": "A result that clears the chance check is evidence, not a promise about future performance.",
              "example": "“B performed better in the test. We'll watch the results as we roll it out.”"
            }
          ],
          "next": "broad"
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "endings": [
    {
      "id": "hold",
      "outcome": "The team keeps A as the default and gathers more evidence before making a final change. This avoids overreacting to the first day's uncertain result, though waiting after a longer test delays a decision supported by the usual chance check."
    },
    {
      "id": "pilot",
      "outcome": "B is tried with a limited share of visitors while the team monitors conversion. In the longer tests, B was 5.0% and A was 4.0%, and the gap cleared the usual 5% chance check; that supports a careful rollout, not a guarantee."
    },
    {
      "id": "broad",
      "outcome": "The team switches everyone to B based on its higher observed rate. After the first day, the evidence was inconclusive; after a longer test, the gap cleared the usual chance check, but no test can promise future results."
    }
  ],
  "summary": [
    "A higher rate in one test group is not enough by itself; check whether chance could explain the gap.",
    "More observations can make a comparison clearer, but waiting also has a cost.",
    "Explain what a test supports without turning evidence into a guarantee."
  ]
}

{
  "title": "A luz chega em ondas ou em pacotes?",
  "setting": "Jardim lunar, noite de festa",
  "mission": "Ajude a equipe a entender o que o sensor está mostrando. **Explique como a luz pode entregar energia em pacotes e também formar um padrão parecido com ondas.**",
  "deadline": null,
  "panels": [],
  "team": [
    {
      "id": "guide",
      "role": "Guia do observatório",
      "expertise": "Conhece a experiência com as duas frestas e quer uma explicação clara para as crianças.",
      "ai": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ai",
      "role": "Assistente de simulação",
      "expertise": "Compara as observações e ajuda a montar testes simples.",
      "ai": true
    }
  ],
  "meters": [
    {
      "id": "clarity",
      "label": "Clareza da explicação",
      "start": 45,
      "goodWhen": "high"
    }
  ],
  "skills": [
    {
      "id": "pacotes",
      "name": "Energia em pacotes",
      "practice": "Explique em uma frase por que a luz pode entregar energia em pequenas porções."
    },
    {
      "id": "dualidade",
      "name": "Onda e partícula",
      "practice": "Conte como a luz pode chegar em pontos separados e, ao mesmo tempo, formar um padrão de ondas."
    }
  ],
  "startNodeId": "teste",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "teste",
      "messages": [
        {
          "from": "guide",
          "text": "A festa precisa da luz dessa esfera para acender pequenos sinalizadores. Quero mostrar às crianças como a luz funciona, mas ainda não sei que observação escolher."
        },
        {
          "from": "ai",
          "text": "Posso ajudar a comparar o que acontece quando observamos chegadas individuais de luz e quando juntamos muitas delas."
        }
      ],
      "prompt": "Como você começa a investigação?",
      "choices": [
        {
          "id": "contar-pontos",
          "text": "Diminuo a luz e peço ao sensor para registrar cada chegada.",
          "quality": "strong",
          "replies": [
            {
              "from": "guide",
              "text": "Boa ideia: assim podemos ver se a energia chega toda de uma vez ou em pequenas porções."
            }
          ],
          "effects": [
            {
              "meter": "clarity",
              "change": 15
            }
          ],
          "timeJump": {
            "label": "Alguns minutos depois",
            "panel": null
          },
          "notes": [
            {
              "skill": "pacotes",
              "kind": "good",
              "text": "Você escolheu observar chegadas individuais, o que ajuda a perceber que a energia da luz vem em porções.",
              "example": null
            }
          ],
          "next": "explicar"
        },
        {
          "id": "olhar-brilho",
          "text": "Observo só o brilho geral da esfera e descrevo o que vejo.",
          "quality": "weak",
          "replies": [
            {
              "from": "guide",
              "text": "O brilho dá uma pista, mas não mostra se a luz chega em porções separadas."
            }
          ],
          "effects": [
            {
              "meter": "clarity",
              "change": -10
            }
          ],
          "timeJump": {
            "label": "Alguns minutos depois",
            "panel": null
          },
          "notes": [
            {
              "skill": "pacotes",
              "kind": "improve",
              "text": "O brilho geral não mostra como a luz entrega energia. Um sensor que registre cada chegada dá uma pista mais útil.",
              "example": "“Vamos registrar os pontos de luz um por um.”"
            }
          ],
          "next": "explicar"
        },
        {
          "id": "pedir-ajuda",
          "text": "Peço à assistente uma comparação entre chegadas individuais e muitas chegadas juntas.",
          "quality": "strong",
          "replies": [
            {
              "from": "ai",
              "text": "Vou comparar os dois registros: pontos separados no sensor e o desenho que aparece quando muitos pontos se acumulam."
            }
          ],
          "effects": [
            {
              "meter": "clarity",
              "change": 10
            }
          ],
          "timeJump": {
            "label": "Alguns minutos depois",
            "panel": null
          },
          "notes": [
            {
              "skill": "dualidade",
              "kind": "good",
              "text": "Você pediu uma comparação que ajuda a enxergar os dois aspectos da luz, em vez de confiar em uma observação só.",
              "example": null
            }
          ],
          "next": "explicar"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "explicar",
      "messages": [
        {
          "from": "guide",
          "text": "O sensor registrou pontos separados, um por vez. Quando a luz passou por duas frestas e muitos pontos se juntaram, apareceu um desenho de faixas claras e escuras."
        },
        {
          "from": "ai",
          "text": "Os pontos mostram chegadas individuais. O desenho acumulado lembra o padrão que ondas podem formar."
        }
      ],
      "prompt": "O que você conta às crianças sobre o que a luz está fazendo?",
      "choices": [
        {
          "id": "faixas-e-pacotes",
          "text": "Explico que a luz chega em pacotes de energia e que muitos pontos podem formar um padrão de ondas.",
          "quality": "strong",
          "replies": [
            {
              "from": "guide",
              "text": "Assim você junta as duas pistas sem dizer que uma delas está errada."
            }
          ],
          "effects": [
            {
              "meter": "clarity",
              "change": 20
            }
          ],
          "timeJump": null,
          "notes": [
            {
              "skill": "pacotes",
              "kind": "good",
              "text": "Você ligou os pontos separados à ideia de que a energia vem em pacotes.",
              "example": null
            },
            {
              "skill": "dualidade",
              "kind": "good",
              "text": "Você explicou tanto as chegadas individuais quanto o padrão parecido com ondas.",
              "example": null
            }
          ],
          "next": "ending-claro"
        },
        {
          "id": "vira-onda",
          "text": "Digo que a luz vira onda quando passa pelas frestas e depois volta a ser pontos.",
          "quality": "fair",
          "replies": [
            {
              "from": "guide",
              "text": "Você notou os dois comportamentos. Só tome cuidado para não sugerir que a luz troca de forma como um objeto que se transforma."
            }
          ],
          "effects": [
            {
              "meter": "clarity",
              "change": 5
            }
          ],
          "timeJump": null,
          "notes": [
            {
              "skill": "dualidade",
